Subject: [PATCH] drivers/ps4: add PS4 Mesa lock verification endpoint
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: multipart/mixed; boundary="------------false"

This is a multi-part message in MIME format.
--------------false
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8; format=fixed
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit


Add /dev/ps4-mesa-lock as a write-only misc device for Mesa/kernel
compat verification using a build-time token.

Userspace writes its compiled-in token, the kernel compares it against
PS4_MESA_LOCK_TOKEN, and returns success only on match. On mismatch,
the write fails with -EPERM and logs 'ps4-mesa-lock: kernel mismatch'.

This provides a simple PS4-specific gate to make patched Mesa abort on
unsupported kernels.

Signed-off-by: Armandas Kvietkus <armandas.kvietkus@proton.me>
---
 drivers/ps4/Makefile        |   7 ++-
 drivers/ps4/ps4-mesa-lock.c | 100 ++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++
 drivers/ps4/ps4-mesa-lock.h |  11 ++++
 3 files changed, 117 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)
 create mode 100644 drivers/ps4/ps4-mesa-lock.c
 create mode 100644 drivers/ps4/ps4-mesa-lock.h


